<!--
  policy_zev_standard.xml : zero-emission car standard as a credit market (RES policy).
  Target: ZEV share of Car passenger-km 10% (2030), 20% (2035), 35% (2040), 50% (2045), 70% (2050).

  DESIGN      Same pattern as the GCAM documentation's renewable/biofuel standard example
              (https://jgcri.github.io/gcam-doc/policies_examples.html, "BioFuelsCredits"):
                - DEMAND for credits: every Car technology consumes a "ZEV_credit" input whose
                  coefficient is the target share.
                - SUPPLY of credits: BEV and FCEV produce credits through res-secondary-output
                  with output-ratio 1 (one credit per unit of their output).
                - POLICY: policy-portfolio-standard name="ZEV_credit", policyType RES. For RES the
                  constraint value is ignored (documentation); the market solves for a credit price
                  that taxes non-ZEVs and subsidises ZEVs until supply of credits >= demand.
              Element names checked in gcam-v9.1: policy_portfolio_standard.cpp (XML name, "RES"
              branch lines 149-150, 205), res_secondary_output.cpp line 71, secondary_output.h line 189.
  UNIT ISSUE  In a tranTechnology the energy-input coefficient is per VEHICLE-km while output (and
              so secondary output) is per PASSENGER-km (output = vkm x loadFactor). To make the
              target a share of pkm, the credit coefficient below is share x loadFactor
              (loadFactor 1.6 assumed; use your base file's Car load factor per technology and year).
              This conversion is the main thing to TEST: check in the output that
              BEV+FCEV pkm / total Car pkm equals the target in binding years.
  SCOPE       One region, the "Car" subsector of trn_pass_road_LDV_4W only. Add the same lines for
              "Large Car and Truck" and "Mini Car" for a full light-duty standard.
  CONFIG      After the "transportation" entry and after any technology add-ons.
  STATUS      Not run in GCAM. Unverified: credit input on tranTechnology (unit handling above);
              whether the RES market clears cleanly in periods where the target is not binding.
-->
<scenario>
  <world>
    <region name="Middle East">
      <policy-portfolio-standard name="ZEV_credit">
        <market>Middle East</market>
        <policyType>RES</policyType>
      </policy-portfolio-standard>
      <supplysector name="trn_pass_road_LDV_4W">
        <tranSubsector name="Car">
          <stub-technology name="Liquids">
